  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National institutions, legal and policy frameworks on social protection strengthened</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria has been facing persistent poverty, inequality and vulnerability challenges despite its economic potential. The COVID-19 pandemic further exacerbated the situation, with unemployment and underemployment on the rise. Inequality, in terms of income and opportunities, is high and adversely affects poverty reduction efforts.  The government is utilizing social protection programmes as an instrument to address the vulnerability of the populace. Despite ongoing efforts to improve the social protection, the coverage, usage and acceptance of these programmes remain relatively low.
The focus of the action is ensuring more people living in Nigeria have increased access to social protection schemes and the strategy includes policy and legal advice, trainings, data interoperability and capacity building. The ILO also participates in the Development Partners Group on Social Protection that facilitates the strengthening social protection system in Nigeria</narrative>
  </description>
